## 5. Decode the public ID when retrieving a job

Later, when the UI calls a status endpoint, decode the ID and query the database using the internal ID.

```
from inflow_outflow.utils.public_job_id import decode_public_job_idfrom inflow_outflow.models.job import Jobdef get_job_by_public_id(session, public_job_id):    decoded = decode_public_job_id(public_job_id)    internal_job_id = int(decoded["id"])    return (        session.query(Job)        .filter(Job.job_id == internal_job_id)        .filter(Job.public_job_id == public_job_id)        .one_or_none()    )
```

The additional `public_job_id` filter ensures the decoded ID matches the stored public ID.

